Considering the disparity in crystallinity and miscibility of the corresponding two blend films, high sensitive external quantum efficiency (s-EQE) measurements of D18-Cl: PYF-T-o- and D18-ChCl: PYF-T-o-based devices were performed to investigate their impact on energetic disorder.[57] As shown in Figure 3a, by linear fitting of the s-EQE spectra beyond the bandgap edge, the Urbach energy \(\left(E_{\mathrm{u}}\right)\) values were calculated to be 24.6 and \(21.5\;\mathrm{meV}\) for D18-Cl- and D18-ChCl-based device. The smaller \(E_{\mathrm{u}}\) implies reduced energetic disorder in the D18-ChCl: PYF-T-o-based devices, which can be attributed to the higher crystallinity and ordered packing of the materials in blend films. The hole energetic disorder \((\sigma)\) was also estimated by temperature-dependent hole transport measurement using the Gauss disorder model (GDM) (Figure 3b,c,d),[58] as expressed in following formula:
